KG42.register("clusters-f33b23c6455fb28d0de384a5",{"id":"07-nash_bargaining::v142-d-K001","paper":"07-nash_bargaining","label":"Electricity trading permission and start-of-day operational responsibilities for microgrids with complementary supply and demand","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"Electricity trading permission and start-of-day operational responsibilities for microgrids with complementary supply and demand","market_meaning":"Where renewable energy surpluses and electricity supply shortfalls complement one another, interconnected microgrids may voluntarily trade electricity, describing the traded object through bilateral quantities for each time slot, with each microgrid operator responsible for start-of-day trading arrangements. Cost improvement is retained as a participation principle; the specific clearing and payment calculations are handled by the second cluster.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["activation","bidding","participation"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The four chains belong to the same interconnected-microgrid mechanism. Supply and demand roles are understood according to the trading situation and are not used to define fixed, mutually exclusive participant categories. This cluster's completeness is limited to qualitative trading permission, product description, and operational responsibilities; exact gain thresholds and actual delivery procedures fall outside the declared scope.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"The two participating parties, the traded object, and the responsible party together form a trading-permission rule that can be understood independently. Assembly follows these complementary meanings, without separately counting the same description of complementary supply and demand as three independent rules for consumers, prosumers, and execution; quantity optimization and benefit allocation remain in the second cluster.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the permitted trading activities and the party responsible at the start of the day, providing this cluster's activity and responsible actor."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplies the participation permission for the demand side with an electricity shortfall in the same trading situation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplies the side providing surplus renewable energy and the principle of voluntary participation; the precise payment constraints associated with the cost principle are referenced through the second cluster."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Specifies the electricity product permitted to be traded and its representation through bilateral quantities for each time slot."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e01"],"rationale":"The candidate quoted passage explicitly describes mutually beneficial trading between microgrids with surpluses and microgrids with electricity shortfalls; the two chains respectively represent the demand and supply sides of this situation."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e01","v141-b-g01-e04"],"rationale":"The same trading situation involving complementary supply and demand is connected from participation permission to the start-of-day trading arrangements for which operators are responsible; this mapping does not additionally assert that physical delivery has occurred."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-X001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::e_ijt","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e01","v141-b-g01-e27"],"rationale":"The product chain and trading-activity chain use the same source-defined bilateral trading quantities for each time slot, respectively expressing the traded object and the trading direction."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O001","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::e_ijt","v141-c-R008::x::v141-c-R008-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27"],"rationale":"The trading parties, time-slot indices, and positive and negative direction conventions in the source are consistent; the local roles in the trading activity and product description, along with their respective unit fields, are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O002","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27"],"rationale":"Both describe the same trading-direction convention, but the frozen expressions respectively use conditional statements and biconditional equivalence. The difference in logical strength is retained, and no representative is selected to replace the originals."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"All B evidence supporting this cluster remains unverified and is used only under this experiment's candidate eligibility; no B source audit, independent C2 review, or Agent E review has been conducted.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e01","v141-b-g01-e04","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g01-e27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the original text, transcription, and interpretation chain by chain; retain the current source status and do not interpret assembled as scientific acceptance."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G002","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The conditional and biconditional formulations of trading direction have not yet been checked for logical strength, and the cited definition excerpt does not separately specify the directional classification of zero trading. The shared positive and negative convention can be used for qualitative assembly, but it is insufficient to eliminate the differences between these two frozen expressions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g02-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the basis for the translation into an equivalence in C and the zero-trading boundary; continue to retain both expressions until confirmation, without fabricating directional criteria."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G003","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The cost-based participation principle in R007-C002 concerns microgrids as a whole but is attached only to the supplier-participation node; R006 does not carry the corresponding economic condition. Proposal v141-b-g02-P01 remains unapproved, and this cluster's assembly cannot be used to restrict the cost principle to a rule exclusive to suppliers.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::participation.consumer","v141-c-R007::V::participation.prosumer","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e06","v141-b-g02-E13"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-P01"],"required_work":"Manually examine the conceptual assignment of the cost-based participation condition; if adjustment is needed, handle it in a subsequent upstream version. For the exact gain threshold, see v142-d-K002-G004 separately."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G004","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The source for R004 supports operators' responsibility for start-of-day trading but does not directly describe the physical execution of cleared trades or confirmation of delivery. There is an interpretive gap between its execution.energy_trade node and the source's responsibility statement.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e04"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the applicability of this node binding; this candidate maintains the boundary of permission and operational responsibilities. If it is extended to actual delivery, additional sources and upstream chains should be supplied separately."}]},"rule_refs":["07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R004","07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R006","07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R007","07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-3fcd5e2d02ec7c3f","COMP-a774da994c2ca212","COMP-d3fb5a9d87fcd5a7","KG31-17257669e6a17fca"]});
